-- title:
--   Gluing local conjugators to a finite idele conjugating lattices
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $\Lambda,\Lambda'$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $D$, each finitely generated and each spanning $D$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (so $\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{Q}}\Lambda=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{Q}}\Lambda'=\top$). For every place $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ write $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$ for the additive subgroup of $D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$, and similarly for $\Lambda'$. Suppose given a family $g_v\in (D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v)^{\times}$ indexed by these places such that (i) for all but finitely many $v$ both $g_v$ and $g_v^{-1}$ lie in $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda'\,v$, and (ii) for every $v$ and every $x\in D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$, one has $x\in\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda\,v$ precisely when $x=g_v\,y\,g_v^{-1}$ for some $y\in\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda'\,v$. Then there is a unit $\beta$ of $D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, whose image under the map [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) induced at $v$ by evaluation of a finite adele at $v$ equals $g_v$ for every $v$, whose inverse $\beta^{-1}$ likewise has $v$-component $g_v^{-1}$ for every $v$, and which satisfies $\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda'\,\beta=\Lambda$: the preimage in $D$, under $d\mapsto d\otimes 1$, of $\beta\,\widehat{\Lambda'}\,\beta^{-1}$ is exactly $\Lambda$, where $\widehat{\Lambda'}=\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}\,\Lambda'$ is the additive subgroup of $D\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes a$ with $z\in\Lambda'$ and $a$ a finite adele integral at every place.
--
--   This is the local-to-global step in the idelic theory of lattices and orders: a coherent family of local conjugators, integral units at almost all places, is the family of components of a single finite idele, and a lattice is recovered from its adelic completion by intersecting with $D$. It is used for the statement that Eichler orders of squarefree level in a quaternion algebra are conjugate by a finite idele, and in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Submodule_exists_units_forall_finiteAdeleEvalAt_eq_conjByFiniteIdele_eq.lean

